          "path": "_m/q/x/m/j/tana-toraja-regency-wp/modern-house-macassar-tana-tor.jpg",
          "filename": "Modern House, Macassar, Tana Toraja 1352.jpg",
          "caption": "In this modern Torajan house, the ground floor is open, as is traditional in SE Asia, to accommodate the family animals\nand other storage space. Living quarters are on the second floor.\nIts corrugated sheet-iron roof is much hotter, but also in the current economy much cheaper and easier to maintain, than any\ntraditional thatched roof. The pediment of the roof is topped by\nX-beams in an almost unimaginably old style, that connects this\n\ntypical modern house to Asian rice granaries from far-away and long-ago.",
          "alt": "In this modern Torajan house, the ground floor is open, as is traditional in SE Asia, to accommodate the family animals\nand other storage space. Living quarters are on the second floor.\nIts corrugated sheet-iron roof is much hotter, but also in the current economy much cheaper and easier to maintain, than any\ntraditional thatched roof. The pediment of the roof is topped by\nX-beams in an almost unimaginably old style, that connects this\n\ntypical modern house to Asian rice granaries from far-away and long-ago.",
          "width": 3072,
